# Ship combat architecture (pointer)

Full law: [`docs/docs/architecture/ship-combat.md`](../../docs/docs/architecture/ship-combat.md).

**Permanent decision:** ship fight loop lives in **Combat** flight mode only.
Hardpoints: **blasters** (semi / burst / full chain) and **missiles** (locking /
non-locking). Hold **RMB** → **10×** combat zoom. Hull combat UI owns blips,
markers, and a lock target card (blue wireframe preview + names + shields/hull).
Contacts show **lead** circles (green hit / red miss). Damage: shields then
hull. Default death: readable **GLB hierarchy break-apart** (not instant
despawn, not extreme debris speed). On-foot firearms stay a separate loop —
[Character combat](../../docs/docs/architecture/character-combat.md).
Flight posture: [Ship flight](../../docs/docs/architecture/ship-flight.md).

When changing ship weapons, lock-on, lead markers, combat zoom, combat HUD,
ship vitals damage, or destruction FX, read the full doc first. Also listed in
`AGENTS.md`.
